ontent.com/Kecksdose/vibe_racer/main/screenshots/race.png","text","mediaReviewed","Screenshot source reviewed","value","2026-10-20","image","gameplay","Creator-published race screenshot from the game repository.","src","/GameMap/media/learning/vibe-racer-opencode.webp","alt","Vibe Racer top-down racing gameplay on a tiled circuit.","https://github.com/Kecksdose/vibe_racer#screenshots","width",1280,"height",720,"credit","Creator-published screenshot","list","attribution","Creator-attributed clients / models (not inferred from related tools)",[88],"OpenCode","Related resources",[93],"resourceIds","section",{"_59":88,"_26":94},"/resources/opencode/","Creator evidence",[98],"evidence",{"_59":99,"_26":100,"_101":102},"See OpenCode and model attribution","https://github.com/Kecksdose/vibe_racer#development","note","Creator disclosure explicitly names OpenCode and GPT 5.2 Codex. The model name does not imply the Codex coding-agent client was used.","Source contents","complete project","Project source",[107],{"_59":108,"_26":109,"_101":110},"Open the complete racing project","https://github.com/Kecksdose/vibe_racer","MIT-licensed game source with supplied maps, replays, screenshots, and pyproject.toml/uv.lock. Python 3.12+; the graphical game needs a local desktop display.","Access type","download","demo","Play or run",[116],{"_59":117,"_26":118,"_101":119},"Download and run Vibe Racer","https://github.com/Kecksdose/vibe_racer/archive/refs/heads/main.zip","No hosted browser build. Requires Python 3.12+ and Pygame 2.6.1+. Run uv run -m src.main; alternatively pip install -e . then python -m src.main. Arrow keys drive, R restarts, G toggles the ghost, and B returns to track selection. Source-checked launch steps; not executed.","Game platform","Source download","Guide format","disclosure","tutorial","Build story / tutorial",[127],{"_59":128,"_26":100,"_101":-7},"Read the tool and model disclosure","Study this workflow","ordered",true,[133,134,135,136],"Download the source and launch the Pygame window with Python 3.12 or newer.","Race a supplied track and compare the player ghost with the unlockable creator ghost.","Read the development disclosure, then inspect movement, lap timing, and replay storage.","Change a track or handling parameter and complete a validation run before saving.","AI workflow / foundation context","Kecksdose names OpenCode as the coding tool and GPT 5.2 Codex as the model. The README publishes a short development disclosure, rather than the original prompts or full conversation.","aiUse","guidance","Creation category","AI-assisted (creator attribution)","category","provenance","Track","2D","track","metadata","Engine","Pygame 2.6 · Python","engine","lead","2d","ai-assisted",[133,134,135,136],{"_59":128,"_26":100,"_18":123},{"_59":117,"_26":118,"_18":112,"_101":119},{"_59":108,"_26":109,"_162":163,"_101":110},{"_59":99,"_26":100,"_101":102},[161],"opencode","scope","complete-project","resource:opencode","resource","An open-source coding agent with multiple model providers, Plan / Build modes, and project instructions.","/resources/",{"_20":161,"_234":88,"_143":235,"_55":236,"_233":166,"_228":227,"_26":225,"_56":237,"_210":238,"_204":239,"_199":240,"_195":194},[171,172,173,174,175,176,177,178,179,180,181,182,183],"website/src/data/resources.json",{"_55":22,"_68":88,"_57":234,"_92":-7},{"_55":152,"_68":166,"_57":233,"_92":-7},{"_55":65,"_59":231,"_68":232,"_57":143,"_92":148},{"_55":65,"_59":229,"_68":230,"_57":55,"_92":148},{"_55":65,"_59":226,"_68":227,"_57":228,"_92":140},{"_55":56,"_59":105,"_61":223,"_57":26,"_92":-7},{"_55":56,"_59":216,"_61":217,"_57":56,"_92":-7},{"_55":84,"_59":208,"_130":197,"_61":209,"_57":210,"_92":-7},{"_55":84,"_59":202,"_130":197,"_61":203,"_57":204,"_92":-7},{"_55":84,"_59":196,"_130":197,"_61":198,"_57":199,"_92":-7},{"_55":65,"_59":193,"_68":194,"_57":195,"_92":148},{"_55":65,"_57":190,"_59":191,"_68":192},{"_55":56,"_57":184,"_59":185,"_61":186},"identitySource","Identity evidence",[